    sized: a linear check of bottom-up deterministic rows before the product check
    
    sized uses the count table when the rows are unambiguous, and
    unambiguousRows builds the product of each pair of states. Rows in which no
    two transitions have the same symbol and child states, as in an e-graph,
    are unambiguous: each term reaches at most one state, so it has at most one
    run. sized now checks that first, in linear time, and builds the product
    only when it fails. For the e-class of a sum of nine variables under
    commutativity and associativity (511 states, 18,678 transitions), the
    product check ran out of a 12 GB heap; with the linear check, ten variables
    (1,023 states, 57,082 transitions) count 17,643,225,600 terms in 0.19
    seconds with 1.2 GB.

